      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "A profound statistical-physics account of how collective motion emerges from local interactions, with concepts now influential across active matter.",
        "attribution": "Vicsek identified the seminal collective-order phenomenon; Toner and Ramaswamy supplied essential hydrodynamic and theoretical foundations.",
        "maturity": "The central predictions and phenomenology have been tested broadly in physical and biological active systems over decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
