        "Charles L. Kane",
        "Eugene J. Mele",
        "Laurens W. Molenkamp"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological-insulator framework revealed a new robust organizing principle for electronic phases.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele provided the defining theoretical proposal, and Molenkamp led decisive experimental realization.",
        "maturity": "The phenomena are firmly established and have seeded a large body of topological-matter research.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The natural boundary between this achievement and the broader topological-matter candidate set requires careful adjudication."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
